Here are easy, no-fuss sightseeing route options starting from Chelsea Hotel Toronto (33 Gerrard St W). I’ve focused on places within a short walk or a quick TTC ride, with Sunday hours in mind.

Option A — Downtown Icons Loop (mostly walking, 5–7 hours)
- Yonge–Dundas Square (7 min walk) and CF Toronto Eaton Centre (open ~11:00–19:00 Sun; quick browse)
- Nathan Phillips Square & Toronto Sign (15 min walk from hotel)
- Art Gallery of Ontario (AGO) (opens ~10:30–17:00 Sun; 20–25 min walk or TTC)
- Kensington Market + Chinatown (great for lunch; 25 min walk from hotel; lively on Sundays)
- TTC to CN Tower/Ripley’s Aquarium (streetcar/subway ~20 min)
- CN Tower (often ~09:00–21:00 Sun; book timed entry to avoid queues)
- Harbourfront Centre/Queens Quay for sunset stroll
Typical timing if you start 10:00: finish ~18:30–19:00. Taxi pickup one hour later: ~19:30–20:00.

Option B — Museums + Midtown Heritage (TTC helps, 6–8 hours)
- Royal Ontario Museum (ROM) (opens ~10:00–17:30 Sun; subway to Museum Station ~15–20 min)
- Yorkville (lunch/shops)
- Casa Loma (opens ~09:30–17:00; last entry ~16:30; from ROM by bus/subway ~20–25 min)
- TTC to Distillery District (boutiques typically open ~10:00–19:00 Sun) OR back downtown for CN Tower evening view
Typical timing if you start 10:00: finish ~18:30–19:30. Taxi pickup: ~19:30–20:30.

Option C — Art, Old Town, and Waterfront (4–6 hours, flexible)
- AGO → Queen St West/Graffiti Alley
- Old Town/Gooderham Building (photo stop)
- Note: St. Lawrence Market South is closed Sundays; nearby cafés/shops are open
- Walk or streetcar to Harbourfront; optional ferry to Toronto Islands if operating and weather permits
Typical timing if you start 11:00: finish ~16:00–17:00. Taxi pickup: ~17:00–18:00.

Key Sunday notes near the hotel
- AGO: ~10:30–17:00
- ROM: ~10:00–17:30
- CN Tower: commonly ~09:00–21:00 (timed tickets recommended)
- Ripley’s Aquarium: commonly ~09:00–21:00
- Casa Loma: ~09:30–17:00 (last entry ~16:30)
- Distillery District: most shops ~10:00–19:00
- CF Toronto Eaton Centre: ~11:00–19:00
- St. Lawrence Market South: closed Sundays

